VoxKeyPaste was inspired by WhisperWriter (https://github.com/savbell/whisper-writer,
GPL-3.0) by savbell. It is an independent implementation written from scratch and
contains no code from WhisperWriter.

The built-in sounds (voxkeypaste/assets/*.wav) are synthesised by tools/make_sounds.py
and the icons by tools/make_icons.py; both are part of this project (MIT).

Third-party software
--------------------
VoxKeyPaste does not include third-party code in this repository. At install time it
uses the following packages, each under its own licence:

  PySide6-Essentials (Qt for Python)  LGPL-3.0-only / GPL-2.0 / GPL-3.0   https://pyside.org
  pynput                               LGPL-3.0                            https://github.com/moses-palmer/pynput
  faster-whisper                       MIT                                 https://github.com/SYSTRAN/faster-whisper
  numpy                                BSD-3-Clause                        https://numpy.org
  sounddevice (bundles PortAudio, MIT) MIT                                 https://github.com/spatialaudio/python-sounddevice
  soundfile (bundles libsndfile, LGPL) BSD-3-Clause                        https://github.com/bastibe/python-soundfile
  pyperclip                            BSD-3-Clause                        https://github.com/asweigart/pyperclip
  webrtcvad-wheels                     MIT                                 https://github.com/daanzu/py-webrtcvad-wheels
  httpx                                BSD-3-Clause                        https://www.python-httpx.org
  PyYAML                               MIT                                 https://pyyaml.org
  pycaw (Windows)                      MIT                                 https://github.com/AndreMiras/pycaw
  comtypes (Windows)                   MIT                                 https://github.com/enthought/comtypes

The Whisper models downloaded by faster-whisper are released by OpenAI under the MIT
License (https://github.com/openai/whisper).

PySide6 and pynput are used as unmodified, dynamically imported libraries, as the LGPL
allows; you can replace them with any compatible version.
